nding of how ideas about language, identity and", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.23931623931623933, "x1": 0.7769230769230769, "y1": 0.25252525252525254}, {"text": "culture are expressed through texts", "x0": 0.21978021978021978, "y0": 0.2556332556332556, "x1": 0.5, "y1": 0.26884226884226886}, {"text": "+ demonstrate understanding of how language is used to shape meaning", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.27583527583527584, "x1": 0.7813186813186813, "y1": 0.289044289044289}, {"text": "about individuals and/or cultural groups", "x0": 0.21978021978021978, "y0": 0.29215229215229216, "x1": 0.5417582417582417, "y1": 0.30536130536130535}, {"text": "+ organise, develop and express your ideas using language appropriate", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.3123543123543124, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.32556332556332557}, {"text": "to audience, purpose and form", "x0": 0.21978021978021978, "y0": 0.32944832944832947, "x1": 0.46373626373626375, "y1": 0.34265734265734266}, {"text": "Question 1 (20 marks)", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.3745143745143745, "x1": 0.3054945054945055, "y1": 0.38694638694638694}, {"text": "A composer\u2019s use of conflict promotes a deeper exploration of identity and culture.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.40792540792540793, "x1": 0.7461538461538462, "y1": 0.4195804195804196}, {"text": "To what extent do you agree with this statement?", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.43745143745143744, "x1": 0.4824175824175824, "y1": 0.44988344988344986}, {"text": "In your response, make detailed reference to the text studied in Module A.", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.4677544677544678, "x1": 0.6681318681318681, "y1": 0.4801864801864802}, {"text": "A list of prescribed texts for Section I is on page 3.", "x0": 0.2703296703296703, "y0": 0.5275835275835276, "x1": 0.6648351648351648, "y1": 0.54001554001554}], [{"text": "The prescribed texts for Section I are:", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.0777000777000777, "x1": 0.42527472527472526, "y